From ffe09e5d4cf372d015d6a0a87d145e807225d5e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Serhii Nikolaichuk <nikolaichuk.s.f@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 07:30:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] go.mod: the releases that fix the vulnerabilities govulncheck
 finds

govulncheck (v1.8.0) found six vulnerabilities that the deployed
programs reach (vts, verification, provisioning, management, coserv,
the sevsnp scheme): GO-2026-6061, GO-2026-6348 and GO-2026-6443 in
google.golang.org/grpc v1.79.3, GO-2026-4394 and GO-2026-6505 in
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk v1.39.0, GO-2026-5970 in golang.org/x/text
v0.37.0. They move to grpc v1.83.2, otel v1.45.0 and x/text v0.41.0, with
what those require; edwards25519 v1.1.1, x/crypto v0.56.0 and x/mod
v0.40.0 too, which fix findings the code does not reach. Left: GO-2026-5932
in x/crypto (no fix released) and GO-2025-3660 in open-policy-agent v0.68.0
(fixed in v1.4.0, a major version), neither reached.
---
 go.mod | 34 +++++++++++------------
 go.sum | 86 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------------------------
 2 files changed, 59 insertions(+), 61 deletions(-)

